{"name":"Skipper","hex":"#748796","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Skipper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A male given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Skipper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea captain","blocks":[{"text":"A sea captain, ship's captain, captain, master, or shipmaster, is a high-grade licensed mariner who holds ultimate command and responsibility of a merchant vessel. The captain is responsible for the safe and efficient operation of the ship, including its seaworthiness, safety and security, cargo operations, navigation, crew management, and legal compliance, and for the persons and cargo on board."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Kristina_Regina_wheelhouse.jpg/330px-Kristina_Regina_wheelhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_captain"},{"title":"Skipper (Barbie)","blocks":[{"text":"Skipper Roberts is a doll created by Mattel in 1964 to be Barbie's young sister. Since 2009, she has had a purple streak in her brown hair and is shown to have a tech-savvy and clever personality. Compared to her sisters, Skipper is introverted and quiet, but also very sarcastic. \\ In some of the Barbie films, she likes to work on her photo blog or DJing. Shes's also level headed and responsible. She had a starring role in the 2023 television film, Barbie: Skipper and the Big Babysitting Adventure."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/Skipper_doll_-_Barbie%27s_little_sister.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skipper_(Barbie)"},{"title":"Skipper (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Skipper is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Dan Skipper, American football player","Elix Skipper, American professional wrestler and former professional football player","George Skipper (1856–1948), English architect","Harry Skipper, Canadian football player","Howard E. Skipper (1915–2006), American cancer researcher and oncologist","John Skipper, American television executive, former president of ESPN","Jim Skipper, American football coach","Katherine Skipper, New Zealand architect","Kelly Skipper, American football coach","Pat Skipper, American actor","Peter Skipper (1958–2019), English footballer","Ricardo Skippers, South African footballer","Ryan Skipper (1981–2007), American murder victim","Spencer Skipper, journalist in South Australia, wrote as \"Hugh Kalyptus\"","Susan Skipper, British actress","Svenn Skipper (1947–2021), Danish composer","Tim Skipper, American vocalist and guitarist in the alternative rock band House of Heroes","Tim Skipper, American football player and coach","Tuzar Skipper, American football player","Wayde Skipper, Australian rules footballer"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skipper_(surname)"},{"title":"Skipper (cannon)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Skipper\" is the name of the Virginia Tech Corps of Cadets' cannon that is sounded at home football games and other events. The game cannon was created by a group of cadets in 1963 for Virginia Tech football games and special events."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Skipper_firing.jpg/330px-Skipper_firing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skipper_(cannon)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/EJ_Smith.jpg/500px-EJ_Smith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/EJ_Smith.jpg/500px-EJ_Smith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Captain of the RMS Titanic, E. J. Smith","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEJ_Smith.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/British_Merchant_Navy_Master_%28Captain%29_Rank.jpg/120px-British_Merchant_Navy_Master_%28Captain%29_Rank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/British_Merchant_Navy_Master_%28Captain%29_Rank.jpg/250px-British_Merchant_Navy_Master_%28Captain%29_Rank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/British_Merchant_Navy_Master_%28Captain%29_Rank.jpg/120px-British_Merchant_Navy_Master_%28Captain%29_Rank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABritish_Merchant_Navy_Master_(Captain)_Rank.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Skipper_Barbie_animated.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Skipper_Barbie_animated.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Skipper's CGI-animated appearance from Barbie Dreamhouse Adventures.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkipper_Barbie_animated.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Skipper_1963_VMI_game.jpg/330px-Skipper_1963_VMI_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Skipper_1963_VMI_game.jpg/330px-Skipper_1963_VMI_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skipper in its inaugural 1963 game: a 35–20 Win over VMI. (Cadets Pictured are Homer Hickam (L) and Butch Harper (R).[6]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkipper_1963_VMI_game.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Workhouse1.jpg/500px-Workhouse1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe